      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T14:53:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e BTW I was just going to ask for this change, so thx for making it :)\n\u003e Dmytro suggested this and I also feel this is a nice optimization :-)\n\n\u003e but my reasoning was a bit different: we should do it directly during unmap by pKVM-low, since compromise host could skip flush hypercall by purpose.\n\nWe partly trust host driver and I think it would not be a security issue to skip flushing. It would affect the functionality and may cause DoS, but should not be a security threat I guess. \n\n\u003e I am also wondering if because of the security issue that I\u0027ve described above there is sense to keep all code related to pkvm_hc_qi_submit_sync since compromised host could always skip it, right? or I am missing some point here?\n\nWe might need to move a considerable chunk of logic to pkvm to remove the hypercall as a whole. The flush queue logic for dma lazy mode, interrupt remaping flush logic etc. It was a tradeoff that we made to make pkvm not so bloated. What do you think?",
