      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T19:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry if I confused you.\n\nWe just need the start address of the page pointed by last_pfn actually. Our goal is to flush `start_pfn` to `last_pfn` inclusive. So now we pass the first address of start_pfn and last_pfn to `pkvm_cache_tag_flush_range`.\n\nIf we look at the implementation of `pkvm_cache_tag_flush_range`, any address with in a page passed as `end` will cause that page to be considered for flushing. `pkvm_cache_tag_flush_range` calls `calculate_psi_aligned_address` and it calculates the nr_pages for flushing as:\n```\nunsigned long pages \u003d aligned_nrpages(start, end - start + 1);\n```\nSo `aligned_nrpages` calculates the number of pages need to cover the address range\n```\n/* Returns a number of VTD pages, but aligned to MM page size */\nstatic inline unsigned long aligned_nrpages(unsigned long host_addr, size_t size)\n{\n»       host_addr \u0026\u003d ~PAGE_MASK;\n»       return PAGE_ALIGN(host_addr + size) \u003e\u003e VTD_PAGE_SHIFT;\n}\n```\n\nSo even if we pass the first address of last_pfn, that page will be counted in nr_pages. \n\nWith your change we pass the last address of `last_pfn`. But since any address in last_pfn can achieve the goal, do we need to do that? What do you think?",
